.TH AENIGMA-TOR-GET-AUTH 8 "2026-08-12" "aenigma-tools 1.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Tools"
.SH NAME
aenigma-tor-get-auth \- display a single Tor client authorization
private key for an onion service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
.B \-s
.I SERVICE_NAME
.B \-u
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
.br
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
.B \-h
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
prints the private Tor client authorization key previously generated
by
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8)
for a single, specified client of a given onion service, so an
operator can retrieve and hand it to that authorized client.
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies that
.IR /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients
exists, and exits with an error if it does not.
.IP \(bu 2
Verifies that
.IR /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth.private
exists, and exits with an error if it does not.
.IP \(bu 2
Prints the private key contents of that single file.
.PP
Only the key belonging to
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
is ever displayed; keys belonging to other clients authorized for
the same service are not read or shown.
.PP
.B aenigma-tor-get-auth
must be run as root, since
.I authorized_clients
and its contents are owned by
.B debian-tor
and are not otherwise readable.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-s " SERVICE_NAME"
Name of the onion service (as configured by
.BR aenigma-tor (8))
that
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
was authorized for. Required.
.TP
.BI \-u " AUTHORIZED_USER"
Name of the authorized client whose private key should be
displayed, matching the
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
originally given to
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8)
when the credential was issued. Required.
.TP
.B \-h
Display a usage summary and exit.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The private key for
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
was found and printed.
.TP
.B 1
Missing
.I \-s
or
.I \-u
argument, the script was not run as root,
.I /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients
does not exist, or no key file exists for the given
.I AUTHORIZED_USER
on that service.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/tor/ SERVICE_NAME /authorized_clients/ AUTHORIZED_USER .auth.private
Private Tor client authorization key for the specified user, read
and printed verbatim to standard output by this script. Not
modified.
.SH EXAMPLES
Display the client authorization private key for user
.I admin
on the
.I aenigma-dashboard
service:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-tor-get-auth \-s aenigma-dashboard \-u admin
.EE
.RE
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
This script prints private key material directly to standard
output. Depending on how the terminal session is configured, output
may be captured in shell history substitutes, terminal scrollback
buffers, screen/tmux logging, or session recording tools, and may be
visible to anyone able to view the screen at the time it is run.
Consider the exposure of the terminal session used before running
this command, particularly over a shared or recorded connection.
.PP
Output is scoped to the single client named by
.IR \-u ;
keys belonging to other clients authorized for the same service are
never read or displayed by a given invocation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR aenigma-tor-auth (8),
.BR aenigma-tor (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
